{"id":"n4-024","title":"Verb た ところ (Verb ta tokoro)","jlptLevel":4,"shortExplanation":"Expresses the situation right after an action has taken place.","longExplanation":"The たところ grammar point is used to describe a situation that occurs right after an action has taken place. It is often translated as 'just now', 'right after', or 'when'. The formation is relatively simple as it only requires the verb in its た form (past tense) followed by ところ.","formation":"Verb (た form) + ところ","examples":[{"jp":"ドアを開けたところ、猫が飛び出してきた。","romaji":"Doa wo aketa tokoro, neko ga tobidashite kita.","en":"When I opened the door, a cat came jumping out.","words":[{"surface":"ドア","vocabId":null},{"surface":"を","vocabId":null},{"surface":"開け","vocabId":"1202450","reading":"あける","baseForm":"開ける"},{"surface":"た","vocabId":null},{"surface":"ところ","vocabId":"1343100","reading":"ところ"},{"surface":"、","vocabId":null},{"surface":"猫","vocabId":"1467640","reading":"ねこ"},{"surface":"が","vocabId":null},{"surface":"飛び出し","vocabId":"2005420","reading":"とびだし","baseForm":"飛び出す"},{"surface":"て","vocabId":null},{"surface":"き","vocabId":"1221520","reading":"き","baseForm":"くる"},{"surface":"た","vocabId":null},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[4]},{"jp":"電話を切ったところ、また鳴った。","romaji":"Denwa wo kitta tokoro, mata natta.","en":"Right after I hung up the phone, it rang again.","words":[{"surface":"電話","vocabId":"1443840","reading":"でんわ"},{"surface":"を","vocabId":null},{"surface":"切っ","vocabId":"1384830","reading":"きる","baseForm":"切る"},{"surface":"た","vocabId":null},{"surface":"ところ","vocabId":"1343100","reading":"ところ"},{"surface":"、","vocabId":null},{"surface":"また","vocabId":null},{"surface":"鳴っ","vocabId":"1532910","reading":"なる","baseForm":"鳴る"},{"surface":"た","vocabId":null},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[4]},{"jp":"宿題を終わらせたところで、友達から連絡が来た。","romaji":"Shukudai wo owaraseta tokoro de, tomodachi kara renraku ga kita.","en":"Just as I finished my homework, I got a message from my friend.","words":[{"surface":"宿題","vocabId":"1337270","reading":"しゅくだい"},{"surface":"を","vocabId":null},{"surface":"終わら","vocabId":"1589600","reading":"おわる","baseForm":"終わる"},{"surface":"せ","vocabId":"2147990","reading":"せ","baseForm":"せる"},{"surface":"た","vocabId":null},{"surface":"ところ","vocabId":"1343100","reading":"ところ"},{"surface":"で","vocabId":null},{"surface":"、","vocabId":null},{"surface":"友達","vocabId":"1540170","reading":"ともだち"},{"surface":"から","vocabId":null},{"surface":"連絡","vocabId":"1559900","reading":"れんらく"},{"surface":"が","vocabId":null},{"surface":"来","vocabId":"1547710","reading":"らい","baseForm":"来る"},{"surface":"た","vocabId":null},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[5]},{"jp":"買い物をして帰ったところ、財布を失くしたことに気づいた。","romaji":"Kaimono wo shite kaetta tokoro, saifu wo nakushita koto ni kizuita.","en":"After shopping and returning home, I realized I had lost my wallet.","words":[{"surface":"買い物","vocabId":"1589730","reading":"かいもの"},{"surface":"を","vocabId":null},{"surface":"し","vocabId":"1310720","reading":"し","baseForm":"する"},{"surface":"て","vocabId":null},{"surface":"帰っ","vocabId":"1221270","reading":"かえる","baseForm":"帰る"},{"surface":"た","vocabId":null},{"surface":"ところ","vocabId":"1343100","reading":"ところ"},{"surface":"、","vocabId":null},{"surface":"財布","vocabId":"1296970","reading":"さいふ"},{"surface":"を","vocabId":null},{"surface":"失","vocabId":"2838586","reading":"しつ"},{"surface":"くし","vocabId":"1244850","reading":"くし","baseForm":"くい"},{"surface":"た","vocabId":null},{"surface":"こと","vocabId":"1313580","reading":"こと"},{"surface":"に","vocabId":null},{"surface":"気づい","vocabId":"1591330","reading":"きづく","baseForm":"気づく"},{"surface":"た","vocabId":null},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[6]}]}